+    "The constructor `QcqpProblem(graph, 1)` creates a QCQP reformulation in which each of the above factors becomes a quadratic cost term in a flattened pose vector (thus D=1), and quadratic constraints make each variable a valid vectorized pose. At a feasible collection of $T^k_w$ poses, the QCQP objective is the same weighted least-squares objective evaluated by the nonlinear graph. This is neither a linearization nor a relaxation of the factor graph: the QCQP is an exact reformulation of its nonlinear objective and pose constraints.\n",
